# Everything in data/ is tracked, and this file is the record of why.
#
# The six files there are what app.R reads, and they are the contract anyone
# rebuilding this dashboard elsewhere consumes. What such a build needs from
# them is provenance - which commit produced these numbers - and a commit
# answers that directly, where a folder sent out of band cannot.
#
# The cost is a copy of two binaries on every refresh, since .rds files store a
# full new object rather than a delta: about 6 MB a refresh, roughly 26 MB a
# year at four refreshes. The four CSVs delta well and cost almost nothing.
# Revisit this if refreshes ever become weekly rather than a few times a year.
#
# Nothing here is confidential: the survey data is published on Dataverse and
# the app is deployed publicly with these files bundled.
#
# Nothing in this directory is ignored, deliberately. A seventh output file
# should be tracked without anyone having to remember to allow it, and an
# explicit list of six is a list that goes out of date silently. OS junk is
# handled by the repository root .gitignore.
